From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pw-pal-plugin: let a source node ask for the PAL raw stream

Every PAL source opens a PAL_STREAM_DEEP_BUFFER stream, whose speaker
mic graph carries the Fluence SMECNS device processing: echo
cancellation and noise suppression remove a tone played on the
speakers, so no node records the microphones as they are. The ACDBs
carry a PAL_STREAM_RAW record graph for that, which nothing can reach.

Open PAL_STREAM_RAW for a source node whose "pal.stream.type" property
is "raw".

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending [to send: AudioReach/audioreach-pipewire-plugin]
---
 src/pw-pal-plugin.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/pw-pal-plugin.c b/src/pw-pal-plugin.c
--- a/src/pw-pal-plugin.c
+++ b/src/pw-pal-plugin.c
@@ -2214,6 +2214,10 @@
                 udata->stream_type = PAL_STREAM_DEEP_BUFFER;
             else
                 udata->stream_type = PAL_STREAM_LOW_LATENCY;
+    } else if (!udata->isplayback &&
+               pw_properties_get(props, "pal.stream.type") &&
+               !strcmp(pw_properties_get(props, "pal.stream.type"), "raw")) {
+        udata->stream_type = PAL_STREAM_RAW;
     } else {
         udata->stream_type = PAL_STREAM_DEEP_BUFFER;
     }
